# The build context of the service images (infra/service-images/Dockerfile) is the repository root.
#
# An allow list: everything is left out, then exactly what the two programs need to compile is let
# back in. Nothing that can hold a secret (infra/compose/secrets, .env files, .git with its history,
# the Claude and editor folders) is ever sent to the Docker daemon, so none can reach a layer.
# Inside what is let in, a file or a folder that is named like a credential is left out too, because
# the build runs every build script of every dependency with the network on and the context is the
# directory, not git: an untracked `.cargo/credentials.toml` would be read there (DR-7). The names are
# those the file system audit of the images calls credentials
# (infra/sandbox-images/tools/fsaudit.py) and a few more.
# infra/service-images/test.sh --static checks that the first rule is "*", that none of the paths
# is let back in, and that the lines after the allow list are exactly the ones listed here, in this
# order. The last rule wins, so a folder is left out after the sources are let back in.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.cargo/
!crates/
!apps/
!xtask/
!schemas/
!migrations/
!docs/database/tests/role_readiness.sql
# Read at compile time by `crates/workflow/src/gates/readability/catalog.rs` (include_str!).
!fixtures/readability/rules.json

# Inside what is let in: files that are named like a credential.
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*secret*
**/*credential*
**/id_rsa*
**/id_dsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.kdbx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/.netrc
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.git-credentials
**/.gitconfig
**/auth.json

# Source files of the programs whose names say "secret" or "credential" because they are the code
# that handles them (crates/egress/src/http/secret.rs, crates/sandbox/src/workspace/secrets.rs).
!**/*secret*.rs
!**/*credential*.rs

# Build output, and folders that hold credentials. After the lines above, so that nothing inside
# them comes back.
**/target
**/.aws
**/.ssh
**/.gnupg
**/.docker
**/.kube
